Overview

The Bio‑Integrity Simulation System (BISS‑v1.0) is a sovereign‑grade biomedical computation engine designed to model human physiology under full encryption while autonomously validating the integrity of every computational transition. It merges:

encrypted physiological modeling

endogenous cryptographic protection

PK/PD simulation

multi‑compartment metabolic dynamics

autonomous suprakernel validation

into a single unified architecture.

BISS‑v1.0 enables tamper‑proof, privacy‑preserving medical computation suitable for clinical research, precision medicine, critical care, and global health modeling.

